Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: complete PCIe hibernation PM callbacks

The PCIe driver puts the firmware and software bus into D3 from its freeze
callback, but does not provide the matching thaw callback. The PCI PM core
does not fall back to the driver's resume callback when a driver PM table is
present and thaw is unset. A test_resume cycle therefore leaves the bus down
after creating the image and fails the second freeze with -EIO.

Use the existing D0 transition for thaw, and pair it with the existing D3
transition for the post-image poweroff phase. This completes the hibernation
callback sequence without changing ordinary suspend/resume behavior.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2872,7 +2872,9 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops brcmf_pciedrvr_pm = {
 	.suspend = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.resume = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
 	.freeze = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
+	.thaw = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
+	.poweroff = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.restore = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
 };
 
